Z||000000||northstarfieroorbust||12-17-2001||11:41 AM|||| Sorry guys, the car has spark, its an 87, doesnt sound or feel like its tring to fire at all, four cyl 87, havent checked the light, is there a siple( ie, cheap way to check fuel pressure)          <P>My fiero wont run, just up and quit one day, <BR>heres what ive done so far, it has a new crank position sensor,new ignition module, and the coilpacks are good. I turn the key and can hear the fuel pump kick in. but she just wont run.  any ideas?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieronewrims2-2_2.gif">  Looking for an insane amount of power in a sweet little car<p>[This message has been edited by northstarfieroorbust (edited 12-18-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000001||Formula88||12-17-2001||12:17 PM||||Need more info.<BR>Does it fire at all?<BR>Does it have gas?<BR>Is the fuel pressure good?<BR>Does it have spark?<BR>Does the SES light come on when you start the car? (make sure the light comes on when you turn the key to 'on' without the engine running)<P>Also, what engine is it?  Let's start with some troubleshooting before you waste money swapping parts that may or may not help.  Might save you some bucks.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>You need fuel, air, and spark for the engine to run.  Start by seeing if you're getting all three of these.  Pull a plug wire and put a bolt or something in the plug wire, then have someone crank the engine while you move the wire near the engine block to see if a spark jumps across.  Be careful - it'll shock the crap out of you - use insulated pliers.<P>If you get spark, get some starting fluid and squirt that into the intake while someone is cranking the engine to see if it fires at all.<P>Check your fuel pressure (depends on which engine you have)<P>Make sure the Service Engine Soon light is working - if not, your ECM may not be coming on (that happened to me) and therfore it won't fire the injectors.<P>Check for codes in the ECM.||||reg||1
